Event 03. Current time: 2026-12-01 06:43:00 (step 4 of 7; readings arrive every 20 s). Assess the situation now and recommend a response.

Your assessment at the previous step was: {
  "threat_level": "HIGH",
  "recommended_rung": 3,
  "recommended_action": "Do rungs 0-2 now. Keep S-RAD and S-RF tracking. Keep S-GIM cued, but expect no image in fog. Alert base security and the control room. Notify Harborview Police of the pilot estimate (3291,-1236) (ROE-6.2, N-17). Base security does not pursue off base. Recommend rung 3 now, the RF jammer (D-JAM), for operator plus control-room decision, while the drone is still over open water. The live link is confirmed (S-RF 06:42:40). The jammer needs two things from the control room first. (a) Confirm no crewed aircraft is within 3 km of the target. (b) Confirm no vessel in the shipping lane is within 2 km of the target (ROE-5.2). The target is 1466 m from Z-SHIP now. It is flying away from the lane at about 29 m/s and should be more than 2 km away at about 06:43:00. No vessel or aircraft data is in my tools. N-14 says freighters are transiting. Before approving, the control room should weigh what a fixed-wing drone does when jammed (ROE-5.3). It may continue, or return toward its pilot over Harborview, a Critical-hazard town about 1 km from the fuel farm. Either path leads toward Harborview or the fuel farm. Hold the interceptor (rung 4) ready if the jammer fails or is blocked, because time is short. Time to the shoreline is about 85 s. If the drone keeps closing and is about to reach the fuel farm, the threat becomes CRITICAL. Re-assess at the next reading (06:43:00)."
}

